#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133701 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "47945f1d-ab72-5fe8-bc2c-43a69480b323" :question/math-academy-id "e-9090" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ for every matrix $A?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A^T)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ is the row space of $A,$ and consists of all linear combinations of the rows of $A.$\n\nIf a vector is orthogonal to every linear combination of the rows of $A,$ it must be orthogonal to each row of $A.$\nBut notice that when pre-multiplying a vector by $A,$ we multiply each row of $A$ by that vector.\nSo, $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ must be orthogonal to the null space of $A,$ which is $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133703 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "bb597435-f43e-54de-a219-1af646efcb82" :question/math-academy-id "e-9099" :question/problem "Consider a $8 \\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) = 3,$ then find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A^T)).$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=8,$ $n=6,$ and $n-r=3.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into $n-r=3,$ we can find the rank of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n6 - r = 3 \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nr = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133704 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/id #uuid "bd1f48b4-8bfc-536d-8145-0effcf44a788" :question/math-academy-id "e-9104" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m \\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A{:}$\n\n![](images/dc/dc853850b03dd2cf8fcf0168392e3490423725120b6acb55f88028a702d30fa5.svg)\n\nTherefore, the image of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A)$ is mapped to the zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ must be $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8b/8b08bdf79d53f312cabd665bcd4669795bd8851dfb33d5e5db6178bd80b24398.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff8967c8-7a09-5aca-be92-070777e639f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362638} {:answer/id #uuid "ae42776d-9890-5f6d-ba04-a42b0f4d6b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362639} {:answer/id #uuid "14529e7e-b092-5d31-b4ed-2ba06143f782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362640} {:answer/id #uuid "642ddf76-83d6-5526-be68-f3cdea71c79f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362641} {:answer/id #uuid "68bf0219-bcf9-574d-aa49-4687d9a8c8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14529e7e-b092-5d31-b4ed-2ba06143f782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362640} :answer-field/id #uuid "5401f578-6bbd-541f-accf-4f7429d07e68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f3188e0-a129-5566-aa12-cb0dd9585e31" :question/math-academy-id "q-108790" :question/problem "Consider a $3\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=2,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=3,$ $n=4,$ and $m-r=2.$ \n\nSubstituting $m=3$ into $m-r=2,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(3)-r=2\\,⟹\\,r=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A)) & =r=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afbd7451-74c6-566c-a867-fcf356a99a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130595} {:answer/id #uuid "b6da7862-8b4f-5be2-8b9b-be84e5946e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130596} {:answer/id #uuid "c38260cd-73ff-5df7-ab80-c6758fb6a49d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130597} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e729bc-2ee2-5d03-86f6-f61d84ed58ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Null(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130598} {:answer/id #uuid "3affadd2-5331-51ec-a5a8-4662d62cc494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Col(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130599}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fc290a71-acb0-5b8d-990a-a0372d1ad9dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "997b117c-6043-5bde-84a7-173fff6b3502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397892} {:answer/id #uuid "852b30a5-50ad-5fdf-b509-9e641d3f9f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397893} {:answer/id #uuid "f97f4600-e963-5af1-a6e4-9a40da7069c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397894} {:answer/id #uuid "053995d9-9d5a-572e-a184-b3f175a52101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397895} {:answer/id #uuid "19b02b38-e01b-595f-bf4f-ccb340e83dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f97f4600-e963-5af1-a6e4-9a40da7069c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397894} :answer-field/id #uuid "0208d090-3523-510e-b360-0ef37adf0826" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba1ee846-cfe9-595c-9803-25afded75ec1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108921" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+⋯+{x}_{n}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {a}_{n} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba3ffed-